WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.680
To the rhythm!

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.720
Check it!

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.690
OK, fellas!

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.910
Yeah yeah party people
let's go let's turn it up

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.790
Let's rush in let's send it flying
let's attack let's dash

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.460
The battlefields are sacred,
Bakuretsu Tenshi, Crazy Burst Angel

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.320
They're a bother, they're cheeky,
come on, blast 'em good!

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.530
Everybody, loosey

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:50.230
Be in full bloom, bluesy

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:53.570
Vividly, crazy

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.070
Fly up, angel

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.380
We are the risma so charisma

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.410
We soar, really prisma (bomber)

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.950
Hey! It's danceable OK
shake it right now let's go

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.750
Gutsiness let's go beat
let's ride the rhythm tension

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.390
It goes flying frustration

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:11.490
Alright let's go let's get it on
loosey beauty get your body

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.990
Everybody, loosey

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:18.500
Be in full bloom, bluesy

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.900
Vividly, crazy

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.960
Fly up, angel

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.530
What are you doing?!

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.520
Stop!

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.370
Howdya like that, jackass?!

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:21.090
Attention, three large motorcycles ahead.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.830
You are in violation of Articles 5
and 8 of the RAPT Traffic Laws.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:31.740
You are advised to pull over and
voluntarily report to the authorities.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:33.860
Outta the damn way!

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.380
You are warned again.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.310
Any further acts of reckless
driving or destruction

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:43.510
will be met with compulsory execution.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:47.350
--Shut up! Stupid cop!
--Die, loser!

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.080
Warning judged as ignored.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.990
Commencing compulsory execution.

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.460
Huh?

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.930
It's fast!

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:17.710
Execution!

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.410
The hell...?!

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:26.120
And you call yourself a cop?!

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.430
Help...!

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:37.970
As you have ignored your warnings
and interfered with official duties,

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:43.410
you will not be granted the right
to a lawyer or a formal trial.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.240
Therefore...

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.510
...execution!

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:52.280
Executions completed.
Removing blockade.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:01.210
We have earned ardent gratitude
from the citizens in response

00:04:01.210 --> 00:04:05.740
to the latest patrol vehicle
we've tested on the Mega Highway.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:08.710
Henceforth, the city of Tokyo
shall continue to strive

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:13.840
for a stable, just government
and pleasant city life.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:20.130
What a weird cop car.
Looks like a praying mantis...

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:23.600
But it has pretty awesome specs!

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:28.190
Its mount during high-speed combat
is at Django's level, maybe higher!

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.680
We have prototypes deployed
at the moment,

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.790
but once we hit mass-production
we'll have a 24-hour system

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:51.020
at each point,
allowing for emergency dispatches.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.630
That's certainly ideal.

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:57.700
As the population increases,
so will the number of lowlifes.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:01.130
From now on, people will
not choose the city;

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.970
the city will choose the people.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.080
I really owe you one!

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.650
I was just thinking about
headin' back to Osaka!

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:21.750
But what a surprise! To think
I'd run into you in Tokyo...

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:25.860
I'm the surprised one! To think
ol' Mika was getting married!

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:30.030
Can't stay a troublemaker forever.
Right, Ta-<i>chan</i>?

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.200
Nope!

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.470
Watch out when you
have lovers' quarrels;

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:36.770
she'll seriously shove
a needle up your nose!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:40.410
--A needle?
--Boss...!

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:45.210
Oops, me and my big mouth! My bad!

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.380
"Traffic Violator"

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.850
"Reckless Driving"

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.650
You don't scare me, cop!

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.550
You don't scare me, cop!

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:41.230
You have ignored your warnings
and obstructed official duties!

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:46.200
Therefore, you will now be
forcefully removed from the road!

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:49.070
Execution!

00:07:02.050 --> 00:07:03.750
Bastard...!

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.600
What is that?!

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:17.940
Ta-<i>chan</i>! Drive safe! Don't let
that thing give us trouble!

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:19.370
I know!

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:24.940
What the...?! What's going on?!

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.480
Not good!

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:31.110
Jump out, you two!

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.820
Boss!

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:49.760
Screw you, you moron cop car!

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:00.870
Boss!

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:09.720
Damn you! You'll pay for this!

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:12.520
Alright! Where's the guy in charge?!

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.760
--Please calm down!
--The hell with that!

00:08:16.760 --> 00:08:20.970
One of your stupid cop cars
busted up my friends!

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:24.260
Go get your head honcho right now!

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:28.040
Number 1 went berserk?

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:31.680
She claims it suddenly attacked
with no warning whatsoever...

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:35.250
That doesn't matter!
Get it back in here!

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:40.550
But if it's true, then it's acting
on its own, outside of our control,

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:42.220
which means..

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.360
Are you saying there's a problem?

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:47.660
I assume you know full well
just how much talent and money

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:52.160
was invested into the
development of the Road Raiders?

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:53.430
Of course.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:58.400
Development of their Third Neurons
was done in top secret,

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:01.770
but their innards are most surprising.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:06.410
You can even call them the final
evolutionary forms science has reached.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:11.080
It was for that belief that I
poured my soul into the project, anyway.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:14.050
We feel the same way.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:17.720
A few sacrifices are to be
expected with scientific progress.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:20.020
If we let ourselves fret over every one,

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:23.150
then our ideal vision for the
future will be but a pipe dream.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:28.000
I'll say it once more.
There is nothing wrong with Number 1!

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.630
Get rid of the dolt at once!

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:34.030
I ain't leaving 'til he comes out!

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:40.380
Oh? Is that the only way
you're gonna respond?

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:42.780
Now things're interesting!

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.150
Perfect!

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:48.690
I'll throttle you lousy Tokyo jerks!

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.680
This means war!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.890
Of all the times...!

00:09:56.890 --> 00:10:00.200
Who's this?! I'm busy right now!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.360
Huh? Where?

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:04.830
Behind me?

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:11.910
Things were gettin' good!
Why'd you stop me?!

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:14.680
The odds looked
pretty stacked against you.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:19.420
Get real! That was my chance
to pound on some Tokyo creeps!

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:23.090
Anyway, I can't just back down now!

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:26.060
The helpless citizens
need retribution, too!

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.330
I don't suppose you could
quietly return to Osaka?

00:10:29.330 --> 00:10:31.300
What for?!

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:35.160
It will be hard to perform our jobs
if we get into trouble with RAPT.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:38.470
This is why I hate Tokyo people.

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:42.640
That's right.
This is Tokyo, not Osaka.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:46.740
There are unseen forces at work.
It's not so simple.

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:51.920
Sure, whatever. I DO have a hankerin'
for some good <i>takoyaki</i>...

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:55.050
I thought you might,
so I got you a ticket!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:57.490
And if I say I won't leave?

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:01.760
Then I'll get you a special seat in
the refrigerator of a long-haul truck.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:03.160
Talk about cruel.

00:11:04.330 --> 00:11:05.900
You're certain?

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:08.900
Yes! We just confirmed it!

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:12.340
Data on Number 1 is being drained.

00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:15.210
--How much?
--Over 50%.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:19.240
The circuits in the RAPT Info
Command Center have been compromised.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.380
Have you tracked down the culprit?

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.550
The hacking is being done
while moving around town.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:26.420
They keep changing relay stations, too.

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:28.940
These are no amateurs.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:35.360
If they're pro hackers, we may have
a new type of terrorist on our hands.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:38.400
Shall I inform the governor
and ask for orders?

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:41.530
No, wait! Not just yet.

00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:43.200
Put Number 1 in the dock.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:48.730
Cut the link with Info Command
before the rest of the data gets stolen.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:28.070
Preparation is underway for
mass-production at private factories.

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:33.780
Please inform the governor
that Numbers 2 and 3

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:35.920
will be rolled out on schedule.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:42.230
Also, Number 1 is undergoing
readjustment for Stage 2 of the project.

00:12:42.230 --> 00:12:46.760
Adjustment? Did an issue
arise during the current stage?

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:52.640
No, it's only needed so we can
record data from practical application.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.330
There are no particular issues...

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:57.160
"Slippery When Wet"

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:03.640
They sure look
like huge gravestones...

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:07.680
The sun seems kinda sad, too...

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:17.950
Screw you, you moron cop car!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.100
Come again?!

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:31.560
Number 1 is ignoring our orders
and is presently on the Mega Highway!

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:35.910
--Is it the hackers' doing?
--I don't know.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.720
Where is Number 1 headed?

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:40.720
Unknown. There's no response
to our calls, either.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.220
Have a chopper follow it
and check the situation!

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:47.820
And keep cars from getting on until
we get the situation under control!

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.310
Are you serious?!

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.950
Yes. I'm sorry.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:13.180
The two units on standby destroyed
their hangar shutters and left!

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:25.930
They appear to be heading
for the Mega Highway, but..

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:27.830
Hello? Hello?!

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:31.390
It can't be... Is Number 1--

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:40.710
This is the place!

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:44.580
This is where the stupid cop car
attacked us last night!

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:47.690
How did it come after you?

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:52.360
I dunno, but it slid right
behind us outta nowhere.

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:55.360
By the time I spun around, it was..

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.730
--Hey, there it is!
--Eh? You serious?!

00:14:57.730 --> 00:15:00.430
Crap! It's attacking again!

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:03.100
No way! We didn't do anything!

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:06.540
That's exactly why
it's a stupid cop car!

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:11.980
--It looks like you're pretty popular...
--Quit joking around!

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:14.750
Attention, large vehicle traveling ahead.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:19.520
One of your passengers is wanted
for obstruction of official duties.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:22.490
Pull over immediately
and follow the orders given.

00:15:22.490 --> 00:15:25.460
In the event you ignore this
warning or attempt to resist,

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:29.360
you will be seen as aiding the escape
of a suspect and be met with force.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:34.790
This doesn't bode well.

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:37.430
Here it comes!

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.440
Eat this!

00:15:47.950 --> 00:15:49.250
Impossible...!

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:54.190
Number 2 hasn't completed its
battle program simulations yet!

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:58.060
I can only assume Number 1
is instructing it.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:01.650
What on earth happened to Number 1?!

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:04.780
What's the deal?

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.270
Yikes...!

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:14.210
--Sei! Don't slow down!
--Jo?!

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:16.140
Smash into the sudden turn

00:16:16.140 --> 00:16:20.110
and open the rear hatch
when I give the word!

00:16:20.110 --> 00:16:21.440
Understood!

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:25.510
Now!

00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:45.900
I knew it! That cop car
was no ordinary cybot!

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:48.770
A glowing brain...

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:50.070
What's she mean?

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:52.940
There was a living brain
in that cop car!

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:57.250
Obviously! I bet some
complete idiot was driving it!

00:16:57.250 --> 00:17:01.190
I already told you,
it's a personified bio-device!

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:03.750
I got NO clue what you're sayin'...

00:17:03.750 --> 00:17:07.060
Still, why do you
suppose it attacked us?

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:12.430
She's right; it might've been
built based off of some crazy guy.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:17.440
My guess is that its
thought control went berserk.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:20.700
Almost like Frankenstein's monster...

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.810
I'd like more data,

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:25.810
but it would be best to
get off the highway for now.

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.350
I don't think that's a choice.

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:31.680
Looks like they still want to play tag!

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:37.220
You're saying Number 1's
target is that large trailer?!

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:40.690
It appears to be an unlicensed vehicle.

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:45.190
It's possible that it's related
to whoever who hacked into us.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:48.800
In which case, that means...

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:52.770
...it's likely Number 1 deemed
that trailer to be dangerous

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:56.370
and acted of its own accord.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:18:01.180
Now I see! Number 1's duty is
to remove suspicious vehicles.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:05.280
And it requested help from
Numbers 2 and 3 to accomplish that...

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:11.190
Indeed. Number 1 is not acting wildly.
It's performing properly!

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.850
Execution!

00:18:36.650 --> 00:18:38.480
Amy! Where's an exit?!

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:40.880
200 meters right!

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:51.320
Hold on!

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.070
Ow...!

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:00.540
Looks like they won't let us out.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:02.570
They trying to shut us up?!

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:05.580
Amy! Can you remove
the lock on the exit?!

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:09.100
I can, but it might take time.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.050
Wow. It opened.

00:19:12.050 --> 00:19:16.210
--Way to go, Amy!
--But I haven't done anything!

00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:20.790
How many are there?!

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:22.120
I'm flooring it!

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:27.030
This is Sky Fish #404.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:30.570
Number 1 is currently in
combat with an unknown cybot.

00:19:30.570 --> 00:19:33.000
Entering Red-Blue Bridge.

00:20:09.270 --> 00:20:14.180
It's no use! I can't
stop it or dodge it!

00:20:14.180 --> 00:20:16.700
Jo! Just you run away!

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:21.590
Sei!

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:24.180
I won't run away!

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:26.390
Jo...?!

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:28.620
Bring it on, Sei!

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.070
Hold on, Sei!

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:40.000
--What're you doing?!
--That's dangerous, Sei!

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.770
Jo! I have faith in you!

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:25.450
Execution... Execution...

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:28.270
Execution...

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:34.090
#404 reporting. Numbers 1
and 3 seriously damaged.

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:38.230
Unknown cybot and trailer
escaping toward the coast.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:40.920
I repeat, Numbers 1 and 3 seriously..

00:21:56.590 --> 00:22:04.260
I remained motionless within the crowd

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:11.900
Not even the voice of my
tears carried on this street

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:19.610
as my feelings of lonesomeness joined it

00:22:19.610 --> 00:22:28.990
In truth, everyone wants
to smile with each other,

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:35.530
yet they get hurt
when they can't do it very well

00:22:35.530 --> 00:22:44.530
But someone will always
be there to watch,

00:22:44.530 --> 00:22:51.410
so let's walk together
beneath this sky

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:16.400
<i>When the crumbling town is
stained red by the evening sun,</i>

00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:20.900
<i>the angel with plucked wings
will fly into the sky once more</i>.

00:23:20.900 --> 00:23:26.710
<i>On the next Burst Angel:</i>
"Bullets in the Iron Grave Post"
